        "Content": "\nBrookview is a beautifully upgraded and exceptionally private contemporary home offering approximately 142 sq. m. of ground-floor accommodation together with an additional c.62 sq. m. of highly versatile, light-filled space at upper level, extending to approximately 203 sq. m. in total, and set on c.0.65 acres of mature landscaped grounds less than 300 metres from the heart of Enniskerry Village.\n\nTucked discreetly behind mature boundaries on the locally renowned Twenty Bends Road, Brookview offers a rare combination of privacy, tranquillity and convenience. The N11 is approximately 2.3 km away, Dublin City 28 km and Dublin Airport around a 40-minute drive.\n\nExtensively upgraded in recent years and presented in superb turn-key condition, Brookview has an immediate sense of calm and seclusion. The private driveway crosses the property's own gently flowing brook before rising towards the house, which enjoys an elevated position surrounded by mature trees, landscaped gardens and sweeping lawns.\n\nA bright and welcoming reception hall with elegant herringbone flooring leads through the principal ground-floor living spaces. To the right is an impressive dual-aspect reception room, ideal as a sitting room, home office, playroom or optional fifth bedroom.\n\nThe ground floor, provides four generous double bedrooms with excellent built-in storage. The principal bedroom benefits from a beautifully appointed en-suite, while a substantial contemporary family bathroom with twin wash-hand basins serves the remaining bedrooms.\n\nAt the heart of the home is the spectacular triple-aspect open-plan kitchen, living and dining room. Bright, beautifully proportioned and designed for both family life and entertaining, the kitchen features Shaker-style cabinetry, silver granite worktops and high-quality NEFF appliances. An oversized granite island incorporating the induction hob and two integrated wine fridges creates a natural gathering point, while a second granite extension provides a generous dining area.\n\nLarge sliding doors open directly onto the patio and gardens, allowing the living space to flow effortlessly outdoors, perfect for summer dining, entertaining or simply enjoying the exceptional privacy and gentle sound of the brook.\n\nUpstairs is an additional c.62 sq. m. of wonderfully bright and versatile space. Flooded with natural light from Velux windows and a large picture window overlooking the gardens, this level comprises two generously proportioned rooms. The spaces could lend themselves particularly well to uses such as home offices, a gym, games or media room, studio, hobby rooms, guest accomodation, master bedroom or additional family space.\n\nA striking contemporary bathroom completes the upper level, while the abundance of natural light and attractive garden outlook give the entire space a particularly bright and appealing character.\n\nBrookview has also benefited from significant recent investment, including triple-glazed windows, external insulation, extensive ceiling and roof insulation and a comprehensively modernised heating system, pipework and pumps.\n\nThe c.0.65 acres of professionally landscaped grounds are among Brookview's most distinctive features. Sweeping lawns, mature trees and established hedgerows provide exceptional year-round privacy, while the property's own brook and spring-fed waterfall bring a wonderful sense of tranquillity to the setting.\n\nA generous patio overlooking the gardens is ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining, while the extensive lawns provide ample space for children, family gatherings and outdoor activities. Despite this remarkable sense of seclusion, Enniskerry Village is less than 300 metres away.\n\nEnniskerry is one of County Wicklow's most picturesque and sought-after villages, offering cafés, shops, restaurants, schools and everyday amenities within easy reach. Bray and Greystones are both within convenient driving distance, while the renowned Powerscourt Estate, with its historic house and gardens, woodland walks, restaurants, shops and championship golf courses, is close by.\n\nFor commuters, the N11 is approximately 2.3 km away, Dublin City approximately 28 km and Dublin Airport around 40 minutes by car, depending on traffic.\n\nBrookview offers a particularly rare combination: approximately 142 sq. m. of beautifully upgraded ground-floor accommodation, complemented by an additional c.62 sq. m. of bright and highly versatile upper-level space, providing approximately 203 sq. m. in total, all set within c.0.65 acres of mature private grounds with its own brook and spring-fed waterfall and with Enniskerry Village virtually on the doorstep.\n\nA superb turn-key family home offering the peace and privacy of a country retreat without sacrificing the convenience of village life.\n\nKey Features\n\n· Less than 300 metres from Enniskerry Village\n· Set on c.0.65 acres of exceptionally private, mature grounds\n· Approximately 142 sq. m. of ground-floor accommodation\n· Additional c.62 sq. m. of bright, versatile upstairs. \n· Approximately 203 sq. m. in total\n· Own brook and spring-fed waterfall\n· Four spacious double bedrooms at ground-floor level\n· Stunning triple-aspect open-plan kitchen, living and dining space\n· Two generous, light-filled rooms at upper level offering excellent flexibility\n· Contemporary bathroom at upper level\n· Triple-glazed windows throughout\n· Extensively upgraded and presented in superb turn-key condition\n· Professionally landscaped gardens with sweeping lawns and mature planting"
      },
